---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Supplement Tracker — Log Daily Doses — Nawtch"
  description="Track daily supplement and approved-medication doses, set per-day targets, and log doses with one tap. All data stays on your device."
  canonicalPath="/supplements/tracker/"
  bodyClass="diets"
>
  <header>
    <div class="header-left">
      <h1>Supplement Tracker</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Log your daily supplement and medication doses against a target.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="date-badge">
      <div class="date-day" id="supp-hdr-date">—</div>
      <div class="date-reset">Resets at midnight</div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <p class="field-hint" style="margin:-4px 0 14px;">Not medical advice — talk to a doctor before starting or changing any supplement or medication routine.</p>

  <div id="supp-tabs"></div>

  <div style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; margin-bottom:12px;">
    <button class="add-btn" id="add-supplement-btn" onclick="window.openSupplementModal(false)">+ Add Supplement</button>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section" id="supp-panel-log">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Your Supplements</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <div id="supplement-cards-list"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="supp-panel-history" hidden>
    <div id="supplement-history-filters"></div>
    <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
      <div id="supplement-history-list"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="info-banners" id="supp-info-banners">
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div
        class="info-banner-header"
        onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')"
      >
        <div
          class="info-dot"
          style="
            background: var(--accent);
            box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--accent);
          "
        ></div>
        <h2 class="info-banner-label">About This Tracker</h2>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        This supplement tracker is a simple daily logging tool for people who want a quick way to keep tabs on
        vitamins, minerals, protein powders, herbs, and routine medications without juggling separate notes,
        calendar reminders, or spreadsheets. It is designed for day-to-day consistency: check your list, mark
        what you took, and see whether you're staying aligned with your target for the day.
        <br /><br />
        Use it to track recurring intake like daily creatine, magnesium, vitamin D, fish oil, caffeine, or a
        prescribed medication schedule. You can set a per-day target for each item, log actual doses as they happen,
        and review your history later to see patterns over time. The tracker is meant to be a lightweight reference
        for your routine, not a substitute for medical advice or a medical record.
        <br /><br />
        Everything you add here is saved locally in your browser, so it stays private to your device and does not
        sync to a server. See the <a href="/supplements/">supplements hub</a> for individual product guides and the <a href="/guides/">guides page</a> for more reference material.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div
        class="info-banner-header"
        onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')"
      >
        <div
          class="info-dot"
          style="
            background: var(--accent);
            box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--accent);
          "
        ></div>
        <h2 class="info-banner-label">How Supplement Tracker Works</h2>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Add a supplement or medication, choose the target amount you want to hit each day, and set the unit that
        matches your routine. You can then log a dose with a single tap, and the tracker keeps your current-day
        total in view so you can quickly see whether you're on pace or already over your target for that item.
        <br /><br />
        The daily status updates automatically as you mark doses, and the history view helps you review what was
        taken on previous days without changing your current plan. If you want a clean reset, you can remove a
        supplement or start again with a fresh list.
        <br /><br />
        Like the rest of Nawtch, this is a local-only tool. Your saved supplement entries stay in this browser only,
        and nothing is sent to a server or account.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="info-banner">
      <div
        class="info-banner-header"
        onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')"
      >
        <div
          class="info-dot"
          style="
            background: var(--accent3);
            box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--accent3);
          "
        ></div>
        <h2 class="info-banner-label">Use It for Daily Consistency</h2>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        This tool is best for keeping a visible record of what you intend to take each day, especially when you are
        juggling several supplements or medications at once. It is useful for checking a routine at a glance,
        spotting gaps, and making it easier to stay consistent over time.
        <br /><br />
        It is not a medical dashboard or diagnosis tool. If you are starting a new supplement, changing a dose, or
        dealing with side effects, talk with a qualified clinician or pharmacist before adjusting your routine.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script src="../../../islands/vanilla/supplements-tracker/tracker.js"></script>
</BaseLayout>
